{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrwqcpUB79i6k1EZsfyJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `Counter` in `metrics/counter.py`. `tests/test_metrics.py` passed on 5 runs in a row. The test only covers lost increments, so the `snapshot()` and `reset()` fixes had no test run against them.\n\n**Root cause:** `incr` read the value, yielded, then wrote it back with no lock. Concurrent increments overwrote each other. `snapshot()` copied the dict while other threads could add keys to it.\n\n**The fix:**\n- **Per-name locks:** each counter name has its own lock, and `incr` holds it for the whole read-modify-write. Unrelated counters never block each other.\n- **Registry lock:** a short lock guards the dict structure. `incr` takes it only for the write, and `get`, `snapshot` and `reset` take it for their dict access. `snapshot()` still returns a plain `dict` copy.\n- **Lock order:** a name lock is always taken before the registry lock, never the reverse, so it can't deadlock.\n- **`reset()`:** `reset(name)` takes that name's lock, so an in-flight `incr` can't write a stale value back after the reset. `reset()` with no argument resets each name in turn, so it is consistent per name but not atomic across all names.\n\nThe API is unchanged. The per-name locks are never removed, so they accumulate for as long as names are used."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14980,"cache_read_input_tokens":41022,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14980},"output_tokens":442,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"faff2e6b-c862-4bae-aabb-9479ecd9a6cb","uuid":"11e7f5f8-be68-4b34-956a-10a8fb9edb6a","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:03:43.852Z","request_id":"req_011CfrwqcXruW9xLQ1C8CZ6b"}
